---

== Ginger Mascarpone Frosting ==

In the bowl of an electric mixer fitted with the paddle attachment, beat @mascarpone cheese{12%ounces}(room temperature), @cream cheese{4%ounces}(room temperature), @confectioners' sugar{2%cups}(sifted), @heavy cream{2%tablespoons}, and @vanilla extract{1/2%teaspoon} together for about ~{1%minute}, until light and fluffy. 

Add @crystallized ginger{1/8%cup}(not in syrup) and @kosher salt{1/4%teaspoon} and beat for ~{30%seconds} more.

== Carrot Cake ==

Preheat the oven to 400°F. 

Line the bottoms of #two 9 x 2-inch round cake pans{} with parchment paper, and grease and flour the pans.

In the bowl of an #electric mixer{} fitted with the paddle attachment, beat @sugar{2%cups}, @vegetable oil{4/3%cups}, and @eggs{3%extra large}(room temperature) on medium-high speed for ~{2%minutes}, until light yellow and thickened. Stir in @vanilla extract{1%teaspoon}.

In another bowl, sift together @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @ground cinnamon{2%teaspoons}, @baking soda{2%teaspoons}, and @kosher salt{1.5%teaspoons}. With the mixer on low, slowly add the dry ingredients to the wet ones.

In a medium bowl, toss @carrots{1%pound}(grated), @raisins{1%cup}, @chopped walnuts{1%cup}, and @all-purpose flour{1%tablespoon}. Stir into the batter with a rubber spatula.

Divide the batter between the prepared pans and smooth the tops. Bake for ~{10%minutes}, lower the heat to 350°F, and bake for ~{30-35%minutes}, until a toothpick comes out clean. Cool in the pans for ~{15%minutes}, turn out onto a baking rack, and cool completely.

Place one cake on a flat serving plate, rounded side down. Spread half the @Ginger Mascarpone Frosting{} on the top (not the sides). Place the second cake on top of the first cake, rounded side up. Frost just the top of the second cake. Sprinkle with @crystallized ginger{}(chopped) and serve at room temperature.